3. Simulation Architecture

3.1 Digital twin state

Define a combined simulation state:
X_t = [x_t,\ z_t,\ E_t,\ T_t,\ m_t,\ b_t]
Where:
   •   x_t: spacecraft navigation state (orbit/attitude)
   •   z_t: subsystem health (latent)
   •   E_t: energy storage state
   •   T_t: thermal state vector
   •   m_t: discrete mode (nominal/degraded/safe/recovery)
   •   b_t: belief state for POMDP policies (optional)

3.2 Module interfaces (clear contracts)

Each module must implement:
   •   Step function: propagate forward one tick
   •   Inputs/outputs: typed interface
   •   Random seed control: reproducible stochasticity
   •   Telemetry: logging all decisions and state variables

