9. Metrics and Success Criteria

9.1 Mission success

Define a mission success indicator:
S = \mathbb{I}[\text{all critical objectives met and no safety violations}]
Estimate probability:
\hat{P}(S=1) = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N} S_i

9.2 Navigation
   •   position error RMS
   •   drift in GPS-denied mode
   •   attitude pointing accuracy
   •   estimator consistency (NEES/NIS if applicable)

9.3 Energy & thermal
   •   constraint violations count
   •   mean thermal margin
   •   battery SOC margin
   •   energy cost per task completed

9.4 Resilience
   •   detection delay distribution
   •   recovery time distribution
   •   mission downtime
   •   mode stability (avoid oscillation between modes)

9.5 Governance & audit
   •   blocked unauthorized actions
   •   audit replay correctness
   •   log hash continuity

⸻

10. Statistical Reporting

For publication-grade reporting:
   •   Report mean ± 95% confidence intervals
   •   Provide distributions (CDFs) for key delays/errors
   •   Use nonparametric tests for robustness comparisons when needed
   •   Publish scenario definitions + seeds + configuration hashes

Example CI for mission success:
\text{CI}_{95\%} \approx \hat{p} \pm 1.96\sqrt{\frac{\hat{p}(1-\hat{p})}{N}}

